meta {
  name: Login
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/_public/v1/users/login
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "password": "Password123!"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 200 && res.getBody().token) {
    bru.setEnvVar("authToken", res.getBody().token);
    if (res.getBody().user && res.getBody().user.id) {
      bru.setEnvVar("userId", res.getBody().user.id);
    }
  }
}

docs {
  # User Login (`LoginUser`)
  
  **Handler**: `handlers.LoginUser` in [auth_handler.go](file:///d:/Codes/budget-tracker/go-server/handlers/auth_handler.go)
  **Route**: `POST /api/_public/v1/users/login` (Public)
  
  ### Description
  Authenticates an existing user and issues a JWT token:
  - Looks up the user account by `email`.
  - Compares provided `password` against the hashed password.
  - On success, generates a signed JWT bearer token containing `user.id`.
  - Returns the sanitized user profile (`id`, `email`, `name`, `username`, `phone`, `avatarUrl`) and `token`.
  
  ### Bruno Automation
  This request includes a post-response script that automatically updates:
  - `{{authToken}}` with the returned JWT token.
  - `{{userId}}` with the authenticated user's ID.
  These variables can directly power all subsequent authenticated Bruno requests under `/api/_private/v1/*`.
}
